  "interpretation": "<div class=\"relative\">\n<div class=\"prose text-pretty dark:prose-invert inline leading-normal break-words min-w-0 [word-break:break-word]\">\n<div class=\"group relative\">\n<div class=\"px-two bg-background border-border shadow-subtle pointer-coarse:opacity-100 right-xs absolute bottom-0 flex gap-2 rounded-lg border py-px opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100\">\n<div>\n<div class=\"flex items-center min-w-0 font-medium gap-1 justify-center\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h2 class=\"mb-xs mt-5 text-base font-[500] first:mt-0 dark:font-[475]\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Reference Ranges* (Typical values; vary by lab and patient demographics)</span></h2>\n<div class=\"group relative\">\n<div class=\"w-full overflow-x-auto md:max-w-[90vw] border-borderMain/50 ring-borderMain/50 divide-borderMain/50 dark:divide-borderMainDark/50 dark:ring-borderMainDark/50 dark:border-borderMainDark/50 bg-transparent\">\n<table class=\"border-borderMain my-[1em] w-full table-auto border\">\n<thead class=\"bg-offset\">\n<tr>\n<th class=\"border-borderMain px-sm py-sm dark:border-borderMainDark break-normal border text-left align-top\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Age Group (Years)</span></th>\n<th class=\"border-borderMain px-sm py-sm dark:border-borderMainDark break-normal border text-left align-top\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Reference Range (ng/mL)</span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Children (Prepubertal)</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">0.05 &ndash; 10.0</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Adolescents</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">0.01 &ndash; 5.0</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Adults</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">0.01 &ndash; 3.0</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"px-two bg-background border-border shadow-subtle pointer-coarse:opacity-100 right-xs absolute bottom-0 flex gap-2 rounded-lg border py-px opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100\">\n<div>\n<div class=\"flex items-center min-w-0 font-medium gap-1 justify-center\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Elevated GH levels</strong> may indicate acromegaly or pituitary adenoma. Further diagnostic evaluation needed.</span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Low GH levels</strong> may suggest growth hormone deficiency; dynamic testing may be required for confirmation.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Random GH levels alone are often insufficient; clinical correlation and dynamic testing recommended.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>",
